{"addedOn":10,"avgRating":["fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o"],"breadcrumbsHtml":"<a href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117\">OpenEdge Development: ABL Reference</a>\n<span><i class=\"fa fa-angle-right\"></i>\n</span>\n<a href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/ABL-Syntax-Reference.html\">ABL Syntax Reference</a>\n<span><i class=\"fa fa-angle-right\"></i>\n</span>\n<span class=\"active\">INPUT CLEAR statement</span>\n","class":"manual","created":1470,"dislikeurl":"https://docs-be.progress.com/dislike/309841","html":"<article class=\"hascomments\" data-page=\"bundle:openedge-abl-reference-117/enus/INPUT-CLEAR-statement.html\" id=\"bundle:openedge-abl-reference-117/enus/INPUT-CLEAR-statement.html\"><main role=\"main\"><article aria-labelledby=\"ariaid-title1\" class=\"dita\" id=\"INPUT-CLEAR-statement\" role=\"article\">\n  <h1 class=\"title topictitle1 reference\" id=\"ariaid-title1\">INPUT CLEAR statement</h1>\n  \n  <div class=\"body refbody\">\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"INPUT-CLEAR-statement__section_N10024_N10021_N10001\">\n      <p class=\"p\">Clears any keystrokes buffered from the keyboard, discarding\nany type-ahead characters. The INPUT CLEAR statement is useful when\nyou want to make sure the AVM clears out extra characters in the\ninput statement that could follow a field entry that is too long.</p>\n      <div class=\"note note note_note\" id=\"INPUT-CLEAR-statement__note_N1002E_N10024_N10021_N10001\"><span class=\"note__title\">Note:</span> Does not apply to SpeedScript programming.</div>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"INPUT-CLEAR-statement__syntax_GC18Q82694578\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d12352e99\">Syntax</h2>\n      \n      <table class=\"table frame-all\" id=\"INPUT-CLEAR-statement__idGDL2K32671601\"><caption></caption><colgroup><col style=\"width:100%\" /></colgroup><tbody class=\"tbody\">\n            <tr class=\"row rowsep-0\">\n              <td class=\"entry colsep-1 rowsep-1\">\n                <pre class=\"pre codeblock\"><code>INPUT CLEAR</code></pre>\n              </td>\n            </tr>\n          </tbody></table>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"INPUT-CLEAR-statement__example_GC18Q92694582\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d12352e125\">Example</h2>\n      \n      <p class=\"p\">This\nmenu procedure tests each key the user presses. If the user presses\na key other than 1, 2, or 3, the AVM clears the keyboard buffer\nand displays a message.</p>\n      <p class=\"p\">\n        <strong class=\"ph b\">r-inclr.p</strong>\n      </p>\n      <table class=\"table frame-all\" id=\"INPUT-CLEAR-statement__idGDL2K42671605\"><caption></caption><colgroup><col style=\"width:100%\" /></colgroup><tbody class=\"tbody\">\n            <tr class=\"row rowsep-0\">\n              <td class=\"entry colsep-1 rowsep-1\">\n                <pre class=\"pre codeblock\"><code>DISPLAY \n  &quot;     Please choose     &quot; SKIP\n  &quot; 1  Run order entry    &quot; SKIP\n  &quot; 2  Run receivables    &quot; SKIP\n  &quot; 3  Exit               &quot; WITH CENTERED FRAME menu.\nREPEAT:\n  READKEY.\n  IF LASTKEY = KEYCODE(&quot;1&quot;) THEN RUN ordentry.\n  ELSE\n  IF LASTKEY = KEYCODE(&quot;2&quot;) THEN RUN receive.\n  ELSE\n  IF LASTKEY = KEYCODE(&quot;3&quot;) THEN QUIT.\n  ELSE DO:\n    MESSAGE &quot;Sorry, that is not a valid choice&quot;.\n  <strong class=\"ph b\">  INPUT CLEAR.</strong>\n  END.\nEND.</code></pre>\n              </td>\n            </tr>\n          </tbody></table>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"INPUT-CLEAR-statement__notes_GC18QA2694588\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d12352e163\">Notes</h2>\n      \n      <ul class=\"ul\">\n        <li class=\"li\">In\nWindows, the keyboard type-ahead buffer can contain a maximum of\n16 characters.</li>\n        <li class=\"li\">If the current input source is not the keyboard, the INPUT CLEAR statement\nhas no effect.</li>\n        <li class=\"li\">INPUT CLEAR is not available on the Windows GUI platform after Progress Version\n7.3D. It is available in Windows character and non-Windows GUI or\ncharacter platforms.</li>\n      </ul>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"INPUT-CLEAR-statement__see-also_GC18QB2694592\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d12352e181\">See also</h2>\n      \n      <p class=\"p\">\n        <a class=\"xref\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"EDITING-phrase.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/EDITING-phrase.html\">EDITING phrase</a>\n      </p>\n    </section>\n  </div>\n<nav role=\"navigation\"><div class=\"familylinks\"><div class=\"previouslink\"><strong>Previous topic:</strong> <a class=\"link\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"INPUT-function.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/INPUT-function.html\">INPUT function</a></div><div class=\"nextlink\"><strong>Next topic:</strong> <a class=\"link\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"INPUT-CLOSE-statement.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/INPUT-CLOSE-statement.html\">INPUT CLOSE statement</a></div></div></nav><nav class=\"related-links\" role=\"navigation\"></nav></article></main></article>\n","isWatched":false,"labelText":"Product; Product > OpenEdge; Product > OpenEdge > Version 11.7; Format; Format > Documentation","likes":0,"likeurl":"https://docs-be.progress.com/like/309841","myDocsURL":null,"numOfPageViews":0,"numOfRatingsText":"<span>0 Ratings","revised":1318,"showWatch":false,"topicMeta":[["bookowner","oe11docs"],["bookrights","oe11docs"],["bundle","openedge-abl-reference-117"],["data","OEInformationHub/Product"],["data","OEInformationHub/Product/product_openedge"],["data","OEInformationHub/Product/product_openedge/product_openedge_117"],["data","OEInformationHub/format"],["data","OEInformationHub/format/format_documentation"],["organization","oe11docs"]],"topicTitle":"INPUT CLEAR statement","topicurl":"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/INPUT-CLEAR-statement.html","type":"Manual"}